      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T20:58:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s the configuration for the SRAM split:\n\n* [Code SRAM](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/baseboard/helipilot/base_board.h;l\u003d95-96;drc\u003d1b8baad8487f1834d41aa1da27a8d500993a2048)\n* [Data SRAM](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/baseboard/helipilot/base_board.h;l\u003d77-81;drc\u003d1b8baad8487f1834d41aa1da27a8d500993a2048)\n\nLooks like we\u0027re currently [limiting RW size] \n(https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/baseboard/helipilot/base_board.h;l\u003d112-119;drc\u003d1b8baad8487f1834d41aa1da27a8d500993a2048) based on SRAM available, not actual Flash available.\n\n(Open question on whether the split is permanent: http://b/329487464.)\n\nI think it still makes sense to make this change so that maybe could take advantage of that extra Flash space this change creates at some point in the future (e.g., choosing to load one of two algorithms from Flash into RAM).",
      "parentUuid": "f2c4d541_25f40e42",
      "revId": "57c7f583d4eb32612a0936f2b59b5de3f50954e6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
