      "writtenOn": "2024-03-14T14:55:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e the older firmware used in the test think the rollback region size is 128KB\n\nMore precisely: RO has hardcoded address where RW starts. If we change rollback size, RW will start at different address.\n\n\nOne more thing about this change. Cortex-M MPU requires the offset alignment to be the same as size of protected region. Currently on helipilot (and bloonchipper) we use 2 MPU regions to protect rollback (because rollback starts at 128KB, and size of both regions is 256KB). With this patch, both rollback regions can be protected with one MPU region.",
      "parentUuid": "e873a3a8_63de2cd0",
      "revId": "57c7f583d4eb32612a0936f2b59b5de3f50954e6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
